## RelayReady protocol

At session start, if `HANDOFF.md` exists:

1. Read it before changing files or acting on the task.
2. Produce the RelayReady 0.1 readback described by `relayready schema readback`.
3. If the `relayready` CLI is available, run `relayready readback check HANDOFF.md READBACK.yaml`.
4. Show the complete readback to the human. Do not continue the task until the human says to proceed.
5. Treat invariants as verbatim constraints. Recheck every stale fact and ask every human-only open question.

Before ending a session with unfinished work, create or update `HANDOFF.md` as an
L1 Writer. Preserve inherited invariants and rejected approaches, then run
`relayready lint HANDOFF.md --check-pointers` when the CLI is available. Never claim
a check ran when it did not.
